    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for module.nodejs-nodemon, nodejs-packaging, module.nodejs-packaging, nodejs-nodemon.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 9.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* undici: Undici Uses Insufficiently Random Values (CVE-2025-22150)\n\n* nodejs: GOAWAY HTTP/2 frames cause memory leak outside heap (CVE-2025-23085)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
